    "rawText": "106 \n17. O₂ Plasma — Organic Material Removal \nPlasma generates: O₂ → O• + O⁺ + other excited species\nThese react with carbon-containing materials to form volatile species such as: CO / CO₂ / H₂O\nO₂ plasma is used for: Photoresist strip • Ashing • Descum • Organic residue removal • Polymer removal\nKey Consideration\nTypical Process / Purpose\nRole of O₂ Plasma\nTarget Material / \nContamination\nApplication\nMost common application\nRemove PR after etch or \nimplantation\nOxidizes organic PR\nPhotoresist\nPhotoresist stripping / \nashing\nMild plasma preferred to protect \nsubstrate\nAfter lithography/develop\nRemoves residual polymer\nThin PR residue\nDescum\nMay require mixed chemistry\nAfter oxide/dielectric RIE\nOxidizes carbon-rich \nresidue\nFluorocarbon CFₓ polymer\nPost-etch polymer \nremoval\nSurface damage must be \ncontrolled\nPre-clean / chamber clean\nConverts carbon to volatile \nproducts\nHydrocarbons / organic \nresidue\nOrganic contamination \nremoval\nHigh removal rate possible\nPattern-transfer processes\nCarbon oxidation\nAmorphous carbon / SOC\nHard-mask removal\nCD control important\nLithography/etch \nintegration\nOxidizes organic BARC\nOrganic bottom anti-reflective \ncoating\nBARC removal\nRate depends strongly on polymer\nMEMS / packaging\nReactive organic etch\nPolyimide, polymers\nPolymer etching\nSidewall/profile control\nAdvanced packaging / RDL\nOxidative removal\nPI\nPolyimide etch/descum\nThickness can require long ash\nPackaging / PCB / RDL\nOxidation\nOrganic resist\nDry-film resist removal\nOften intentionally modifies only \nsurface\nAdhesion improvement\nCreates polar functional \ngroups\nPolymer surface\nSurface activation\nAvoid overexposure\nBefore deposition/bonding\nRemoves carbon \ncontamination\nOrganic monolayers/residue\nSurface cleaning\nSurface chemistry is critical\nMEMS / wafer bonding\nCleans/activates surface\nOrganic contamination\nWafer bonding \npreparation\nDepends on deposited material\nRIE/PECVD chamber PM\nOxidizes carbon deposits\nOrganic chamber deposits\nChamber cleaning\nDescum: remove only residual PR at the bottom of developed features. \nAshing: remove essentially the whole photoresist layer. \nO₂ RIE: intentionally pattern/etch an organic \nlayer with directional ion assistance.\n \n",
