    "rawText": "103 \nSummary\n•\nLithography = Key Patterning Process\nTransfers circuit patterns onto the wafer and determines resolution, CD, overlay, pattern fidelity and yield. \n•\nSurface Preparation & Adhesion\nDehydration Bake + HMDS remove surface moisture and improve photoresist adhesion. \n•\nPhotoresist & ARC Materials\nPositive/Negative PR, CAR, BARC/TARC, PI/PBO are selected according to wavelength, resolution, film \nthickness and application. \n•\nCoating & Exposure Control\nPR thickness/uniformity and exposure dose, wavelength, focus & alignment are critical to achieving the \ntarget pattern. \n•\nDevelopment & Pattern Formation\nTMAH (typically 2.38 wt%) is a key developer for positive PR; development conditions directly affect CD \nand pattern profile. \n•\nStrip, Rework & Process Control\nPGMEA, NMP/DMSO-based and formulated strippers support PR removal/rework, while metrology verifies \nCD/CDU, overlay and defects before subsequent processing. \nSuccessful Lithography = Right Material + Right Chemical + Right Process + Right Pattern + Right Control\nClean → Prime → Coat → Bake → Align/Expose → PEB → Develop → Inspect → Etch/Implant → Strip\n",
