    "rawText": "10 \nWhy Is CMP needed in Semiconductor \nManufacturing? \nCMP is essential for achieving a highly planar wafer surface, controlling film thickness, and \nenabling reliable multilayer device fabrication.\nKey Purposes of CMP\n1.\nSurface Planarization: Removes surface topography and reduces height variations caused \nby deposition, etching, and patterning.\n2. Multilayer Integration: Provides a flat surface for subsequent lithography and thin-film \ndeposition in advanced semiconductor devices.\n3. Improved Lithography: Minimizes focus variation and depth-of-focus (DOF) limitations, \nimproving pattern resolution and overlay performance.\n4. Selective Material Removal: Removes excess materials while retaining desired structures, \nsuch as Cu interconnects, W plugs, and shallow trench isolation (STI).\n5. Film Thickness Control: Achieves uniform dielectric and metal film thickness across the \nwafer.\n6. Improved Device Yield and Reliability: Reduces topography-related defects, electrical \nfailures, and process variability.\n",
