    "rawText": "29 \nDielectric Planarization CMP \nOxide Surface Planarization \nRemove excess dielectric material and eliminate surface topography \nto achieve a highly planar wafer surface for subsequent lithography, \nthin-film deposition, and multilayer semiconductor fabrication.\nProcess Principle\n•\nDielectric Deposition: Deposit SiO₂-based dielectric films (e.g., \nPECVD SiO₂, TEOS oxide, or HDP-CVD oxide) over patterned \nstructures, creating surface topography.\n•\nCMP Planarization: Remove raised dielectric regions through \nchemical reactions and mechanical abrasion.\n•\nSurface Leveling: Higher regions experience greater initial material \nremoval, reducing height variations across the wafer.\n•\nThickness Control: Control the final dielectric thickness, within-\nwafer uniformity, and surface planarity.\n",
